<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Saint Titus</h1><p class="st-meta">1363 CE – 1364 CE · capital Candia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Rebel republic proclaimed by Venetian colonists in Crete in 1363, which briefly united Latin and Greek Cretans against Venice.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1363 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> demanded a new tax from the feudal settlers of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venetian-crete">Venetian Crete</a> to pay for repairs to the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a>. The colonists, already resentful at being excluded from power in Venice, rebelled under leaders including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-gradenigo">Marco Gradenigo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tito-venier">Tito Venier</a>, imprisoned the Venetian duke and proclaimed independence under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/titus-saint">Saint Titus</a>, patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The rebels formed a government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a> led by a governor and councillors. To win Greek support they made concessions to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> church and drew in Greek nobles such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kallergis-family">Kallergis family</a>. Their republic lacked outside allies: the pope and other powers backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> sent a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luchino-dal-verme">Luchino dal Verme</a>, which retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heraklion">Candia</a> in May 1364. Leaders were executed and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-the-evangelist">Saint Mark's</a> banner restored, though Greek rebels led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kallergis-family">Kallergis</a> brothers fought on until 1367.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-saint-titus.jpg" alt="Republic of Saint Titus" width="320" height="410"><figcaption>Image: Marco Boschini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MBoschini_Il_regno_tutto_di_Candia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1363 CE – 1364 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Candia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Marco Gradenigo, Tito Venier</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Venetian, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Revolt of Saint Titus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1364&amp;focus=republic-of-saint-titus" aria-label="Republic of Saint Titus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5236 759 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Saint Titus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5636 1157h0M5293 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5556 1015h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5556 1015h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Greece. <a href="/atlas?year=1364&amp;focus=republic-of-saint-titus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
